  "section_notes": "The final text keeps the 5% figure for S2 only as a regulatory review threshold, with no mandatory sales stop, which substantially protects Northwind's Hearth 10 (6.2%). S3 sets new-unit shut-off at 24 months and retrofit at 6 years, both favouring Northwind's low coverage (38%), while S4 (36 months) favours Halcyon's suppression costs; S5 keeps a model-specific 8/100k mandatory recall that bites on Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9/100k), though it is framed as a remedy rather than a sales ban. Customers receive per-model failure rates under S2, but public publication is excluded, so both companies' red lines were respected."
